  "narrative": "The new validation evidence resolves the central question and upgrades the supplied-dataset conclusion from one robust marker-like association to two. First, H39 is confirmed: feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 is associated with a much higher outcome_014 CRISPR dependency score. The discovery estimate was +0.796 with 95% interval +0.776 to +0.816, and independent validation was +0.829 with interval +0.800 to +0.857. Using the approximate absolute 10% threshold around the outcome_014 mean, about 0.0093, this is an enormous effect and remains far above the threshold in both discovery and validation. Because more negative dependency scores indicate stronger dependency, the positive exposed-minus-comparator contrast means feature_027=1 is associated with weaker outcome_014 dependency, not stronger vulnerability.\n\nSecond, H77 validation confirms the opposite-direction discovery for feature_021 and outcome_006. H77 registered the negative/vulnerability direction, and its independently signed estimate is -0.786 with interval -0.815 to -0.757; that rejects the registered negative contrast. The corresponding direction-reversal claim H89 is positive and robust: discovery +0.802 with interval +0.782 to +0.822 and validation +0.786 with interval +0.757 to +0.815. This is also far above the approximate outcome_006 absolute 10% threshold of about 0.0093. I therefore reject and close H77 as the original registered negative claim, while accepting H89 as the correct dataset-internal association. As with outcome_014, higher values mean weaker dependency, so feature_021=1 is associated with much weaker outcome_006 dependency relative to feature_021=0.\n\nThe H15 validation closes feature_060-outcome_014 as an unsupported association. Its validation estimate was essentially zero, 0.000089 with interval -0.048 to +0.048, which includes zero and both clinically meaningful and clinically negligible values. I therefore reject and close H15.\n\nThe overall positive findin